---
/**
 * The title band on an inner page: the same right-attached column the homepage
 * opens with, sitting over whatever backdrop the page has installed.
 *
 * It carries no photograph of its own. On these pages the picture is fixed to
 * the viewport by the layout's `backdrop` slot and stays still while the
 * content scrolls over it, so a second copy inside this section would scroll
 * away and tear away from the one behind it.
 *
 * A full-screen hero was the option rejected at mockup. Someone arriving at an
 * inner page has come to read something, usually after scanning a printed card
 * outdoors; making them scroll a viewport of scenery first is brand continuity
 * bought with the reader's time.
 *
 * `-mt-28 pt-28` is the same cancelling pair the homepage uses: the band has to
 * start behind the header, which `BaseLayout` renders above the page slot and
 * the page cannot reach. Pull the section up by the header's height, pad the
 * contents back down by the same amount, and neither element needs to know the
 * other's size. Pages using this must pass `heroOverlay` to `BaseLayout`, which
 * is what drops the header's divider — a hairline ruled across a photo reads as
 * a rendering defect.
 */
interface Props {
  title: string;
  lead?: string;
}

const { title, lead } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="relative -mt-28 flex min-h-96 flex-col overflow-hidden pt-28">
  {/*
    A local halo on top of the page-wide wash: the band is where the photograph
    is busiest and where the largest type sits, so the title needs more cover
    than the cards below it do.

    Radial and anchored on the title rather than a linear ramp. A linear one
    stops dead at the band's bottom edge and rules a visible horizontal seam
    across the photograph — it was built that way first and the seam is why it
    isn't now. This fades out in every direction, so the band has no edge.
  */}
  <div
    class="absolute inset-0 bg-radial-[at_78%_45%] from-sand/85 via-sand/40 to-transparent"
  >
  </div>

  <div class="relative mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-1 items-center px-4 py-10">
    <div class="max-w-xl">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-brand sm:text-5xl">{title}</h1>
      {/* The shorter measure keeps the line endings off the busiest part of the
          photograph, the same reason the homepage's lead carries it. */}
      {lead && <p class="mt-4 max-w-md text-lg">{lead}</p>}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
